		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>In todays data-driven world, effectively organizing and presenting data is challenging, particularly for non-experts. Although tables organize data systematically, they often fall short in conveying intuitive insights; in contrast, charts provide clear and compelling visual summaries. Although recent advances in NLP, powered by large language models (LLMs), have primarily benefited high-resource languages such as English, low-resource languages such as Bengali spoken by millions worldwide still face significant data limitations. This research addresses this gap by introducing &quot;Bengali Chart-Summ,&quot; a benchmark dataset with 4,100 Bengali chart images, metadata, and summaries. This dataset facilitates the analysis of LLMs (mT5, BanglaT5, Gemma) in Bengali chart-totext summarization, offering essential baselines and evaluations that enhance NLP research for low-resource languages.</p>
			</abstract>
